Wait — in the 10th frame, after the first roll:
- If the first roll is a strike (10): pins_standing resets to 10, and the player gets two bonus rolls.
- Otherwise: pins_standing = 10 - pins, and the second roll is the second roll of the frame.

After the second roll:
- If pins_standing (before the roll) was 10 (i.e., the first was a strike): after the second roll, if the second is also a strike, pins_standing resets to 10 and a third roll is needed; otherwise pins_standing = 10 - pins and the game ends (no more rolls even if it's a spare — "scoring a strike or spare on a fill ball does not grant the player additional fill balls").
- If pins_standing was less than 10 (the first was not a strike): the second roll must be ≤ pins_standing; game ends.

So the rule for the 10th frame: after the second roll, if pins_standing was 10 and pins == 10 (a strike), a third roll is allowed. Otherwise the game ends.

